# HBCO core TBox — CONSOLIDATED into the OntoSage Conversational Building Vocabulary (OCBV).
#
# As of OCBV 2.0.0 the canonical, publication-ready definitions of the hbco: conversation concepts
# (hbco:Concept, hbco:CompositeConcept, hbco:mapsToBrickClass, hbco:layTerm, …) and their SHACL
# shape live in ONE file:
#     input/ontosage_schema.ttl   (Module B + Module I)
# so the whole "talk to the building" layer is a single document. The hbco: namespace and every
# term are unchanged — this consolidation is non-breaking.
#
# This file is intentionally kept (as a valid, near-empty stub) so tooling that globs ontology/*.ttl
# still finds it, without duplicating the TBox (which would risk drift between two copies).
# Per-building lay-term instances live in ontology/hbco_mappings.ttl and input/<bldg>_concepts.ttl
# and resolve against the terms defined in input/ontosage_schema.ttl.

@prefix hbco:    <http://ontosage.org/hbco#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

hbco:Concept rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://ontosage.org/ontology> .
